From: Armada <armada@armadaos.dev>
Subject: [PATCH] freedreno/a8xx: emit an RB_DONE_TS event after each draw

On the A830, DOOM (2016) with the OpenGL renderer still hung the GPU every
one to six minutes of gameplay with 0016 applied, often during screen
flashes or particle effects. It only hangs with GMEM rendering: sysmem
never hangs. Disabling binning, LRZ, UBWC or the GMEM fast paths didn't
help, and neither did turnip-style resolve groups, a WFI around every
GMEM load, clear and store, or bigger VPC buffers.

An RB_DONE_TS event that writes memory after each draw stops it: no hang
in 17 minutes of play across two runs, plus 19 minutes with a debug build
that also had it. These all still hang: a CP_MEM_WRITE before each draw,
the event without a write, the event after every 8th draw, and a
CCU_CLEAN_DEPTH after each draw. The cost is about 1 fps (135 vs 136).

Only A8xx gets the event, so other GPUs see no change.
---
diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a6xx/fd6_context.h b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a6xx/fd6_context.h
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a6xx/fd6_context.h
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a6xx/fd6_context.h
@@ -161,6 +161,9 @@ struct fd6_control {
    } flush_base[4];
 
    uint32_t vsc_state[32];
+
+   /* written by the RB_DONE_TS event after each draw on A8xx: */
+   uint32_t draw_done;
 };
 
 #define control_ptr(fd6_ctx, member)                                           \
diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a6xx/fd6_draw.cc b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a6xx/fd6_draw.cc
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a6xx/fd6_draw.cc
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a6xx/fd6_draw.cc
@@ -556,6 +556,27 @@ draw_vbos(struct fd_context *ctx, const struct pipe_draw_info *info,
 
    flush_streamout<CHIP>(ctx, cs, &emit);
 
+   /* On A830, GMEM rendering hangs the GPU every few minutes in DOOM (2016),
+    * usually during bursts of small blended draws. An RB_DONE_TS event that
+    * writes memory after each draw prevents it. A CP_MEM_WRITE before each
+    * draw, the event without the write, or the event after every 8th draw
+    * all still hang.
+    */
+   if (CHIP >= A8XX) {
+      fd_pkt7(cs, CP_EVENT_WRITE7, 4)
+         .add(CP_EVENT_WRITE7_0(
+            .event = RB_DONE_TS,
+            .write_src = EV_WRITE_USER_32B,
+            .write_dst = EV_DST_RAM,
+            .write_enabled = true,
+         ))
+         .add(CP_EVENT_WRITE_ADDR(
+            .bo = fd6_ctx->control_mem,
+            .bo_offset = offsetof(struct fd6_control, draw_done),
+         ))
+         .add(ctx->batch->num_draws);
+   }
+
    fd_context_all_clean(ctx);
 }
 
